    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Portugal built the first sea-borne trading empire linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#africa">Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#asia">Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#americas">Americas</a>, starting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ceuta">Ceuta</a> in 1415.</li><li>It controlled the spice route around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#africa">Africa</a> and became the largest national carrier in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#dutch">Dutch</a> rivals, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#grito-do-ipiranga">Brazilian independence</a> and colonial wars wore it down; the last territory, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#macau">Macau</a>, went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a> in 1999.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Portuguese traders who landed on Tanegashima in 1543 introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#arquebus">arquebus</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#japan">Japan</a>, where gunsmiths quickly copied it and changed Sengoku-era warfare.</p></aside>
    </section>

